+What:		/sys/class/misc/transmeta-ptt/state
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		(RO) State of the Persistent Translation Technology (PTT)
+		service of the Transmeta Crusoe Code Morphing Software: load,
+		save, saveok, saved, error, idle, off, keygen, nokey or unknown.
+		nokey means the boot ROM holds no valid PTT key for this
+		processor, PTT is then not usable.
+
+What:		/sys/class/misc/transmeta-ptt/version
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		(RO) PTT version CMS implements, "2.0" for CMS 4.4.0.
+
+What:		/sys/class/misc/transmeta-ptt/stats
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		(RO) CMS PTT counters since the last load, one "name value" line
+		each:
+
+		=================== ==========================================
+		installed           translations installed from the database
+		installed_discarded installed translations discarded again
+		new                 new translations that a save exports
+		new_discarded       exportable translations discarded again
+		new_unfiltered      new translations outside filter_pid
+		other_discarded     other discarded translations
+		loaded              translations in the loaded database
+		=================== ==========================================
+
+What:		/sys/class/misc/transmeta-ptt/last_load
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		(RO) 0 when the last load through /dev/transmeta-ptt succeeded,
+		otherwise its negative errno, e.g. -74 (EBADMSG) for a database
+		CMS rejected.
+
+What:		/sys/class/misc/transmeta-ptt/abort
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		(WO, root only) Writing 1 abandons a save or load CMS still
+		holds and returns it to the idle state; -EBUSY while
+		/dev/transmeta-ptt is open.
+
+What:		/sys/class/misc/transmeta-ptt/filter_pid
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		(RW, root only) Writing a process id makes CMS mark only the
+		translations made while that process's address space runs as
+		exportable, so the next save holds the code of that program.
+		The filter is the page table base of the address space at the
+		time of the write and does not follow an exec. 0 exports all
+		translations (default).
+
+What:		/sys/class/misc/transmeta-ptt/keygen
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.2
+Contact:	René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
+Description:
+		(WO, root only) Present only with the module parameter
+		allow_keygen=1 (default off). Writing the value
+		"program-boot-rom" makes CMS generate a new PTT key and
+		PROGRAM IT INTO THE BOOT ROM; any other value is rejected
+		with -EINVAL. The driver never generates a key by itself,
+		also not in state nokey. A failed ROM write can leave the
+		system unbootable; databases saved with an older key are no
+		longer accepted.
